{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21879366",
      "title": "More Fun with Named Routes & Location Objects",
      "lectureOrder": 181,
      "videoOrder": 157,
      "sourceHash": "ac502557c5d49189e5dd01d2ff7130ddcd9806f1d3ae228ec2bdc44b69e3a71b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.24,
          "end": 4.56,
          "en": "So now we learned about nested routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.56,
          "end": 8.97,
          "en": "Now imagine a bigger view application where you have dozens,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.97,
          "end": 11.66,
          "en": "or maybe even hundreds of different routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.66,
          "end": 14.81,
          "en": "some routes deeply nested in our routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.81,
          "end": 17.46,
          "en": "You can also have multiple levels of nesting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.46,
          "end": 20.9,
          "en": "you could have children here on this nested route as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.9,
          "end": 22.46,
          "en": "So imagine an application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.46,
          "end": 25.65,
          "en": "where you have a lot of such nested routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.65,
          "end": 27.6,
          "en": "If you have such an app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.6,
          "end": 30.583,
          "en": "constructing links like recurrently doing it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.03,
          "end": 34.73,
          "en": "like this, can quickly become cumbersome,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.73,
          "end": 37.89,
          "en": "you always have to add the full path here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.89,
          "end": 39.04,
          "en": "and build it out like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.04,
          "end": 41.1,
          "en": "You have to build such a long string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.1,
          "end": 43.963,
          "en": "which describes the path you wanna navigate to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.14,
          "end": 48.09,
          "en": "Now, because this can get cumbersome,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.09,
          "end": 52.46,
          "en": "the view router offers two very useful features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.46,
          "end": 55,
          "en": "which make building such links,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55,
          "end": 57.983,
          "en": "which we pass to router link more convenient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.15,
          "end": 61.42,
          "en": "The first useful feature which we have,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.42,
          "end": 65.16,
          "en": "is the fact that the two prop on router link,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.16,
          "end": 68.42,
          "en": "does not just take such a string link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.42,
          "end": 71.56,
          "en": "It does take that, but not just.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.56,
          "end": 74.9,
          "en": "Besides passing such a string which holds the path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.9,
          "end": 79.34,
          "en": "you can also use an object as a value for two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.34,
          "end": 80.36,
          "en": "For that, of course you need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.36,
          "end": 82.783,
          "en": "to bind two dynamically with a colon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.7,
          "end": 88.64,
          "en": "And then this object may have various options,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.64,
          "end": 91.82,
          "en": "that allow you to describe the route you wanna load.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.82,
          "end": 96.13,
          "en": "In this object, you can set a path property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.13,
          "end": 97.7,
          "en": "and that then takes a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.7,
          "end": 101.50999999999999,
          "en": "which could be slashed teams plus this ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.50999999999999,
          "end": 104.15,
          "en": "so what you returned as a string before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.15,
          "end": 106.68,
          "en": "Now, by just doing that, we of course don't gain much.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.68,
          "end": 108.75,
          "en": "We basically do what we did before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.75,
          "end": 111.22,
          "en": "but now inside of an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.22,
          "end": 112.81,
          "en": "This gets more useful,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.81,
          "end": 115.17,
          "en": "if we combine it with another nice feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.17,
          "end": 119.49000000000001,
          "en": "the view router offers, and that would be named routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.49000000000001,
          "end": 122.503,
          "en": "We can assign a name to every route which we have,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123.45,
          "end": 127.77,
          "en": "simply by adding a name property to the route config.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.77,
          "end": 130.443,
          "en": "Here for example, we could name the route, teams.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.29,
          "end": 134.713,
          "en": "We could name this nested route here as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.79,
          "end": 137.96,
          "en": "team dash members, maybe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.96,
          "end": 139.52,
          "en": "The names are totally up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.52,
          "end": 141.143,
          "en": "they just should be strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.39,
          "end": 144.18,
          "en": "So now I assigned two names,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.18,
          "end": 147.34,
          "en": "and of course you can assign names to any routes you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.34,
          "end": 150.653,
          "en": "And now we can leverage that name, team members.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 151.75,
          "end": 154.79,
          "en": "Back in the teams item component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.79,
          "end": 158.5,
          "en": "now instead of setting the path property, which we can do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.5,
          "end": 162.66,
          "en": "we can at the name property on this route location object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.66,
          "end": 164.56,
          "en": "which we pass to two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 164.56,
          "end": 167.62,
          "en": "And here we can use team dash members for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.62,
          "end": 170.7,
          "en": "making it clear that this router link,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.7,
          "end": 173.9,
          "en": "should load this nested route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.9,
          "end": 177.03,
          "en": "Of course, this route has a dynamic segment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177.03,
          "end": 178.93,
          "en": "so we should also set this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.93,
          "end": 182.58,
          "en": "And we do that by adding a second property to this object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 182.58,
          "end": 185.28,
          "en": "which describes the destination we wanna go to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.28,
          "end": 187.71,
          "en": "And that's the params property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 187.71,
          "end": 189.34,
          "en": "Params takes an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 189.34,
          "end": 192.82,
          "en": "where you now can set up your params as key value pairs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.82,
          "end": 194.31,
          "en": "And of course, I mean the params,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 194.31,
          "end": 197.63,
          "en": "which are expected by the route with that name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 197.63,
          "end": 198.63,
          "en": "So in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198.63,
          "end": 201.73,
          "en": "that team members route once a team ID param,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 201.73,
          "end": 205.28,
          "en": "because that's the name we chose here as a dynamic segment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 205.28,
          "end": 209.13,
          "en": "hence here, we can add team ID in this nested object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 209.13,
          "end": 210.63,
          "en": "which we provide to params,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 210.63,
          "end": 213.303,
          "en": "and then set our value here to this ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 214.89,
          "end": 218.23,
          "en": "Now arguably, that's a bit more code than before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 218.23,
          "end": 221.9,
          "en": "but it actually has two great advantages I would say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 221.9,
          "end": 224.24,
          "en": "It's very readable and maintainable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 224.24,
          "end": 227.2,
          "en": "and it has one extra huge advantage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 227.2,
          "end": 229.31,
          "en": "If you ever should decide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 229.31,
          "end": 231.65,
          "en": "that you wanna go with a different path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 231.65,
          "end": 234.573,
          "en": "let's say team instead of teams,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 235.62,
          "end": 240.62,
          "en": "then you don't need to go to this team item component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 240.65,
          "end": 244.2,
          "en": "and update the path everywhere where you used it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 244.2,
          "end": 246.04,
          "en": "instead, the name didn't change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 246.04,
          "end": 248.67,
          "en": "So you don't need to update anything here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 248.67,
          "end": 251.67,
          "en": "and you can still conveniently change the path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 251.67,
          "end": 253.49,
          "en": "how often you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 253.49,
          "end": 257.84,
          "en": "That's why navigating by name instead of by path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 257.84,
          "end": 261.36,
          "en": "might be a useful pattern, especially of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 261.36,
          "end": 264.26,
          "en": "in bigger applications where you use a route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 264.26,
          "end": 266.72,
          "en": "in a lot of different components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 266.72,
          "end": 269.43,
          "en": "You then don't have to update all those components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 269.43,
          "end": 271.733,
          "en": "whenever you decide to change the path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 273.21,
          "end": 275.67,
          "en": "And that's why passing such an object instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 275.67,
          "end": 278.88,
          "en": "of a string to two, can be useful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 278.88,
          "end": 281.54,
          "en": "By the way, you can provide the same object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 281.54,
          "end": 284.08,
          "en": "to this router push,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 284.08,
          "end": 287.03,
          "en": "in case you should be navigating programmatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 287.03,
          "end": 291.46,
          "en": "You can provide the same kind of object to this push method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 291.46,
          "end": 292.89300000000003,
          "en": "but that's just a side note.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 294.39,
          "end": 298.23,
          "en": "And if I do that and save everything, and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 298.23,
          "end": 301.4,
          "en": "our links here, therefore still work fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 301.4,
          "end": 304.89,
          "en": "And I can load different team members now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 304.89,
          "end": 307.38,
          "en": "bypassing this object to two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 307.38,
          "end": 310.2,
          "en": "And the view router will analyze this object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 310.2,
          "end": 312.3,
          "en": "compare it to your route set up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 312.3,
          "end": 314.7,
          "en": "and create the correct anchor tech,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 314.7,
          "end": 316.09,
          "en": "with the correct link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 316.09,
          "end": 319.593,
          "en": "to and to be loaded route and therefore component.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
